<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gleb Vasilkovich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1237–1278</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gleb Vasilkovich was the first prince of Beloozero, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> separated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> in 1238 after his father Vasilko of Rostov was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. He cooperated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, married a Mongol princess and later also ruled Rostov.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gleb-vasilkovich.jpg" alt="Gleb Vasilkovich" width="320" height="590" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s Facial Chronicle (Illustrated Chronicle of Ivan the Terrible) (... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%93%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%B1_%D0%92%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87_%D0%B8_%D0%A4%D1%91%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%80_%D0%A7%D1%91%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%B8_%D0%BA%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B3%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8F_%D0%A4%D1%91%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
